{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/396849-what-happened-to-gorool","id":396849,"title":"What happened to Gorool?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-07T15:37:15-08:00","id":396849,"title":"What happened to Gorool?","content":"How, exactly, was Gorool defeated?<br /> <br /> Was it destroyed, or is it still around?<br /> <br /> Was it Gorool's destruction that killed Charon (as it held the essence of Charon's Shadow)? Or vice versa?<br /> <br /> <br /> Was Charon able to face the Malfean because if held the essence of his Shadow?<br /> <br /> Would the two still have the same relationship as a Ferryman to their discarded Shadow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T16:34:37-08:00","id":396907,"title":"","content":"Unknown, just like the hows and whys of Charon's reincarnation after he threw himself into that whirlpool in the Weeping Bay. Unlike Charon, Gorool never returned after the 5GM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T22:49:49-08:00","id":397222,"title":"","content":"Oracles suspected that Charon won Gorool by reincarnating them both into the mortal world, They were trying to find them both as they hoped that through the death of Charons reincarnation Charon might return and worried that should the same happen to Gorools incarnation it would return. So Gorool might still be around. It's left open.<br /> <br /> Charon was able to face him because he was The Man, aside from that while he did face it in the sense that he managed to get close without being killed and he managed to stand against it for a small while his intention was never to fight it as such but to use whatever trick he used to open up the reincarnation whirlpool. He knew when he rose up to face Gorool that he wouldn't return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T13:11:44-08:00","id":397929,"title":"","content":"It is rumored that Gorool is The Wyrm. So if Charon destroyed the Wyrm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T13:24:06-08:00","id":397964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/396849-what-happened-to-gorool?p=397929#post397929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is rumored that Gorool is The Wyrm. So if Charon destroyed the Wyrm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait what? It's a big Malfean thing, which is something the Garou would consider to be of the Wyrm if they ever encountered it. But Gorool being the actual Wyrm, 'member of the Triat' Wyrm? No.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T13:35:42-08:00","id":397977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/396849-what-happened-to-gorool?p=397929#post397929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is rumored that Gorool is The Wyrm. So if Charon destroyed the Wyrm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait! What? When? Where? How?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T13:37:09-08:00","id":397979,"title":"","content":"Didn't Gorool chow down on Charon's Pasiphae? (Or more like &quot;devour/encompass/become&quot;) Maybe the matter/anti-matter Ferryman/Pasiphae interaction played a part in the whole &quot;resurrection hot tub&quot; thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T13:44:53-08:00","id":397982,"title":"","content":"I believe it was actually his Shadow for the ritual used was a Castigation one. Though, for my part, I've discarded that Anubis Ritual Thing and keep it some manner of Castigation Secret Uber-Ritual instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T14:02:18-08:00","id":397998,"title":"","content":"If Charon was a Ferryman,aren't his Shadow and his Pasiphae the same thing? <br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure the Ferryman material wasn't written when &quot;Gorool ate his Shadow&quot; was first mentioned. So &quot;Gorool ate his Shadow&quot; would be the way to encompass that thought, as Pasiohae weren't a thing yet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T14:29:23-08:00","id":398059,"title":"","content":"Charon refused to partake of the Ritual that the other Ferrymen took that separated their shadow from themselves, thusly creating the Pasiphae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T07:54:14-08:00","id":398761,"title":"","content":"True, Charon never went through the Ferryman rite and so never had a Pasiphae his Shadow broke away when the Pardoners were trying to Castigate it through the use of a Castigate 5 power that brings forth the shadow as a separate entity that is still physically linked to the Psyche and Charons Shadow managed to brake free.<br /> <br /> And no Gorool has never, to my knowledge at least, been compared to the Wyrm only Oblivion has and even in that case in the end they are two separate things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T12:08:38-08:00","id":399131,"title":"","content":"I did say it was rumored. The book mentions that the Wyrm is an active force of destruction and corruption while Oblivion is patient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T13:09:40-08:00","id":399211,"title":"","content":"That does make me ponder, How does Werewolf Cosmology deal with Oblivion? Its not prat O' their Triat...though it is also something they don't really deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:01:41-08:00","id":399270,"title":"","content":"I think they regard spectres as Wyrm-tainted even though said spectres would disagree about what exactly they're infected with/serve. It seems to me that the personification of the Wyrm and the impersonal, internal nature of Oblivion are just two different ways of looking at the same cosmic principle, and a distinction is being made based on the sort of spirit entities aligned to that overarching concept that each splat encounters in their respective levels of reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:42:06-08:00","id":399373,"title":"","content":"From what I gather the Wyrm, though corrupt now is a natural cycle of destruction that allows for the creation of new things. Oblivion on the other hand is Complete destruction of existence and a totally separate entity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:49:23-08:00","id":399386,"title":"","content":"Oblivion is seen in much the same way by the Euthanatos Tradition, a necessary breaking down of spiritual leftovers that's necessary for renewal and reincarnation. And Wraith really isn't all that definite on Oblivion being an entity at all, some viewpoints speculate about it as a natural inclination of the universe that some self-destructive ghosts want to speed up. Like I said, I think it's just various people putting their own slant on the same concept of entropy, based on what sort of agents of entropy they're familiar with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T22:51:20-08:00","id":400015,"title":"","content":"He went on to play the Balrog in Ralph Bakshi's version of Lord of the Rings, struggled to find work, got a job as a barista until he met a handsome blond fellow named Antonio and now spends his days playing house boy for Antonio and his partner Roger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T10:51:31-07:00","id":437228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mental-Mouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/396849-what-happened-to-gorool?p=399373#post399373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I gather the Wyrm, though corrupt now is a natural cycle of destruction that allows for the creation of new things. Oblivion on the other hand is Complete destruction of existence and a totally separate entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, actually, Orpheus reveals that Oblivion does destroy in order to create. And it's occasionally hinted that Transcendence and Oblivion might both end in pretty much the same thing: souls being reincarnated/recycled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T11:01:48-07:00","id":446189,"title":"","content":"from a demon the fallen perspective(i know different game but still..) transcendence would be&quot;that secret fate meant for humans alone&quot;<br /> <br /> a wraith book(core i think) explicitly states that the wyrm represents active entropy while oblivion is passive.<br /> <br /> if oblivion and transcendence are the same then what is the point in this whole conflict? why is oblivion so corrupt?<br /> 2 sides of the same coin perhaps but not the same in my opinion.<br /> <br /> just like descension and ascension in mage are certainly not the exact same thing.<br /> <br /> by the way does anyone else find it stupid that charon was as strong as a neverborn? the mightiest one in fact. beings that created demon lords by dreaming<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 03-17-2015, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T11:49:24-07:00","id":446340,"title":"","content":"To be fair, my impression from the early descriptions of that conflict were that Charon managed some Hail Mary Pass kind of trick to neutralize Gorool and himself at the same time, not that they were necessarily equal opponents. Then again, the Wraith line reducing the enemy bosses of the Werewolf and Mage lines to the imaginary friends of its big antagonists never sat well with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T12:08:39-07:00","id":446352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/396849-what-happened-to-gorool?p=446340#post446340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, my impression from the early descriptions of that conflict were that Charon managed some Hail Mary Pass kind of trick to neutralize Gorool and himself at the same time, not that they were necessarily equal opponents. Then again, the Wraith line reducing the enemy bosses of the Werewolf and Mage lines to the imaginary friends of its big antagonists never sat well with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wraith didn't do that. Mage did (Book of Madness Revised).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T17:18:15-07:00","id":446762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/396849-what-happened-to-gorool?p=446189#post446189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> by the way does anyone else find it stupid that charon was as strong as a neverborn? the mightiest one in fact. beings that created demon lords by dreaming</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like the sort of thing a PC does....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T17:29:10-07:00","id":446769,"title":"","content":"Yeah I got to go with Matt on this. To me it always seemed like Charon was luring Gorool into a trap, sacrificing himself to save Stygia. I don't ever recall anything about Charon being as strong as Gorool, in fact the nature of how the two went out would imply that he isn't as strong as the Neverborn as he basically sacrificed himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T20:32:46-07:00","id":446991,"title":"","content":"It HAD to be a trick... He took off his mask, laid down his scythe, etc. He was divesting himself of all of his objects of power. So he would have to be PERSONALLY as powerful or Gorool, or he had to have had an angle. One of those, &quot;I jump in and die... but then nobody else does&quot; kinda angles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T21:52:18-07:00","id":447128,"title":"","content":"Didn't the Lady of Fate basically tell him long before that Gorool would come and that he would met his end only to be reborn and eventually return for the 6GM?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T23:02:53-07:00","id":447180,"title":"","content":"isnt him a space tree who cant say anything other than his name, who also fights next to a space rocket and Batista from WWE?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T00:15:46-07:00","id":447266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/396849-what-happened-to-gorool?p=447128#post447128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't the Lady of Fate basically tell him long before that Gorool would come and that he would met his end only to be reborn and eventually return for the 6GM?</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Ends of Empire (specifically Guildbook Mnemoi), the Oracles' Guild foretold Charon's eventual destruction at the hands of a Malfean and Stygia's end in a subsequent Great Maelstrom.<br /> <br /> Charon's destruction was a fixed event, something that could not be averted. However, the Oracles also said that Charon could force the matter, changing when it happened, thus enabling him to find a way to the Skinlands.<br /> <br /> That is, it wasn't a given he would come back; he had to change things to enable his rebirth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T02:40:26-07:00","id":561732,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I always hated that Gorool was this finite, limited thing. Wraith had always made it quite clear that if a Malfean awoke, reality would be obliterated.<br /> <br /> My ruling on this was either that Gorool was a onceborn/hekatonkhire or that in swallowing Charon's shadow, it become something less than a Malfean. <br /> <br /> I always saw the Malfeans' consciousness/awareness of reality as the thing that was dangerous. Like the Red King in Through the Looking Glass, they have to be kept sleeping. Perhaps Gorool's Malfean mind remained sleeping and it was Charon's shadow that animated its bloated monstrous form. That's the only way I can reconcile the Gorool incident with what we know about the Malfeans.<br /> <br /> Orpheus made things worse by stating previously Onceborn Malfeans were actually Neverborn, and then turned Grandmother into the Ultimate Bad.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, though, I inferred from the cosmology section of Mage 20 that God is Prime, and has an equal and opposite in The Adversary/Oblivion (as a matter and anti-matter duality). Mage further suggests both might be aspects of the same entity or primal force. As Demon often refers to God as a She, and Grandmother is an anthropomorphicised aspect of Oblivion, it's entirely possible that they're the same thing (Grandmother is God, Oblivion is Prime, and the universe is the Ouroboros). It perhaps explains where God disappeared to in Demon (Her consciousness inhabited The End instead of The Beginning, as She readied herself for annihilating Creation).<br /> <br /> I've read way too much into this, of course...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T04:33:58-07:00","id":561773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/396849-what-happened-to-gorool?p=561732#post561732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I always hated that Gorool was this finite, limited thing. Wraith had always made it quite clear that if a Malfean awoke, reality would be obliterated.<br /> <br /> My ruling on this was either that Gorool was a onceborn/hekatonkhire or that in swallowing Charon's shadow, it become something less than a Malfean.<br /> <br /> I always saw the Malfeans' consciousness/awareness of reality as the thing that was dangerous. Like the Red King in Through the Looking Glass, they have to be kept sleeping. Perhaps Gorool's Malfean mind remained sleeping and it was Charon's shadow that animated its bloated monstrous form. That's the only way I can reconcile the Gorool incident with what we know about the Malfeans.<br /> <br /> Orpheus made things worse by stating previously Onceborn Malfeans were actually Neverborn, and then turned Grandmother into the Ultimate Bad.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, though, I inferred from the cosmology section of Mage 20 that God is Prime, and has an equal and opposite in The Adversary/Oblivion (as a matter and anti-matter duality). Mage further suggests both might be aspects of the same entity or primal force. As Demon often refers to God as a She, and Grandmother is an anthropomorphicised aspect of Oblivion, it's entirely possible that they're the same thing (Grandmother is God, Oblivion is Prime, and the universe is the Ouroboros). It perhaps explains where God disappeared to in Demon (Her consciousness inhabited The End instead of The Beginning, as She readied herself for annihilating Creation).<br /> <br /> I've read way too much into this, of course...</div> </div> </div> </div>Doomslayers has active Neverborn. On page 95, after discussing how the vast majority of Neverborn slumber in their temples, it then says: &quot;Some very few of the Neverborn are more active than this. For them, dreaming of the day when they too may be consumed in the soothing embrace of Oblivion is not enough. These walk or creep or crawl the passageways of the Labyrinth, seeking to speed the day of the final dissolution by their personal efforts.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then there's Rabark the Inhabited on page 100. &quot;Also called The Tree That Blossoms Inward, Rabark is the rarest of all evils: an active Neverborn.&quot;<br /> <br /> Where did Wraith say that if the Malfeans awoke, reality would be obliterated?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T08:18:17-07:00","id":563038,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure. I feel like it's in the core book. I'll have to check when I get home. It could just be that I've assumed that, perhaps by conflating them with the Children of Clanbook: Baali (whom I've always thought sounded like primordials in the Exalted sense). <br /> <br /> The Wraith books seem inconsistent in their treatment of the Neverborn. One minute they're primal forces of nature. The next, they're just really big spectres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T16:15:44-07:00","id":563490,"title":"","content":"I always just seen the Malfeans as really powerful eldritch horrors... The Neverborn at least. Onceborn to me are the 'really big Spectre' variety. I still want some confirmation if Grandma and Oblivion are one and the same.<br /> <br /> I've never seen Malfeans awakening causing the end of reality... Wraith had Oblivion spreading and threatening to eat all of reality, though I never saw Malfeans as sleeping gods/demons. I saw them as the dark horrors responsible for the Labyrinth (as written in Wraith 1e... Just how the early Malfeans link to Demons we can talk about another time). Just why they never really ventured up through the Tempest so much makes me wonder about them though.<br /> <br /> And yes, I do see the Malfeans as the Primordials from Exalted that then went to become the Neverborn. Same as I picture Malfeas being the same realm that holds the Wyrm as the one that held the Yozi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T17:55:24-07:00","id":565900,"title":"","content":"p.275 of WTO, Second Edition: <br /> <br /> 'Malfeans rarely emerge from the Labyrinth, and when they do, their appearance signals some great impending catastrophe. It is rumored that somewhere in the darkest recesses of the Labyrinth dream Malfeans who have slept since time began, of whom Gorool itself was but a pale imitation. Should ever they awaken, then surely the Final Maelstrom shall break over the Shadowlands, and Oblivion will reign over all.' <br /> <br /> I'm not sure where I got that other idea from. Although, curiously, the above description might presage Grandmother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T10:58:31-07:00","id":566695,"title":"","content":"I doubt there will be definitive word on Grandmother's origin/nature, if it appears at all in Wraith 20. The Orpheus line went out of its way to present several different options and purposefully avoided committing to any one as the definitive answer.<br /> <br /> (Personally I always favored the surviving-ghost-of-a-dead-universe that somehow latched onto the WoD's still-living one option, as Grandmother's actions seemed a little too concrete and active to be the work of Oblivion as a principle, and it suffered too many limitations and setbacks in struggles with lesser beings to be an omnipotent negative reflection of God.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T08:45:11-07:00","id":568039,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that passage does sound like Grandma before she was a thing... Seems some element of her was planned for the metaplot, I'd say. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So Grandma could have been basically an Exalted Malfean in so many words? I need to really delve back in to Orpheus, I was always more interested in the Underworld geography as shown in Wraith, with the changes in Orpheus and the corporate angle of it, I found it less my thing really.<br /> The idea of the Stormwall did bring up the frankly cool Spectral Hives though and there were always Nihils, though I was not a fan of the Shadowlands and the Underworld being taken out of the gameline's focus.<br /> <br /> Well, because Wraith 20 will be reversing things back, I believe Grandma will be asleep still (if she is mentioned at all) and the big enemy between all Wraiths and Orpheus will more centrally be the corrupted growth of Oblivion and Spectres. I'd be interested to see more stuff between how the three factions of Hierarchy, Renegades and Heretics would react to the Orpheus Group projecting into the Shadowlands and maybe even the Tempest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T08:18:52-07:00","id":592643,"title":"","content":"For me, Grandmother doesn't fit the themes of Wraith because she is a reimagining of them. She plays up on a few things: the alien natures of the Neverborn and the sick, dysfunctional family nature of the Spectre hivemind. But wraith is about endings, and Oblivion is one of the endings of your identity; the annihilation forced on you if you cannot choose willing Transcendence. It can have no identity, no motivation, it is just the inevitable end of all things. That's what makes the Neverborn so monstrous, that they are the reversal of that process. They perfectly counterpoint the existence of Wraiths because they never lived and want to die. <br /> <br /> The alien life that wants to share its life with everything, though? Well its not anathema to Wraith but it doesn't really fit either. At least not as a force greater than the Neverborn.<br /> <br /> Orpheus, though, is not about endings but about new lives. So the existential threat that ends all choice becomes a death of identity rather than the final end. The inescapable Grand Maw of Oblivion becomes the inexorable Grandma. Still the price of giving up, still a potential ending for your story, but itself a new life. The worst new life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T10:27:56-07:00","id":600694,"title":"","content":"The way I see it: if we see Charon again, Gorool is just as likely still around. Kinda yin-yang in that sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}